            "n_events": 29,
            "result_text": "I've created `/app/filter.py` with a robust JavaScript removal filter. Here's what it does:\n\n**JavaScript removal features:**\n1. **Removes `<script>` tags** - Eliminates all `<script>...</script>` blocks with their content, including any attributes on the script tag\n2. **Removes event handlers** - Strips out dangerous attributes like `onclick`, `onload`, `onerror`, `onmouseover`, etc. (anything matching `on*=...`)\n3. **Removes `javascript:` protocol URLs** - Cleans up dangerous URLs in attributes like `href`, `src`, `action`, `data`, `background`, `poster`, `formaction`\n\n**Design principles:**\n- Uses regex patterns to surgically remove only dangerous content\n- Preserves all HTML structure, formatting, attributes, and content\n- Processes files in-place as requested\n- Handles both quoted and unquoted attribute values\n- Case-insensitive matching for HTML tags and protocols\n\n**Usage:**\n```bash\npython filter.py input.html\n```\n\nThe script will modify the file in-place, removing all JavaScript while keeping the rest of the HTML intact."
